Sotto does not bundle a speech model, an engine or ffmpeg. scripts/install.sh installs them
on your Mac from their own sources, under their own licenses:

  Phonon-2 speech model     Fermion Research. CC BY 4.0.
                            https://www.fermionresearch.com/research/phonon-2/
                            https://huggingface.co/FermionResearch/Phonon-2
  fermion-research          Fermion Research: the `phonon` CLI and speech engine. Apache License 2.0.
                            https://github.com/fermionresearch/phonon
  ffmpeg                    The FFmpeg developers. LGPL/GPL, installed with Homebrew.
  Caddy (optional)          Apache License 2.0, installed with Homebrew.

The web app includes, through its npm dependencies:

  Hono, @hono/bun, fflate, React, Base UI, shadcn/ui, Tailwind CSS, Sonner    MIT
  Lucide icons                                                                ISC
  Geist, Geist Mono (Vercel), Literata (TypeTogether), via Fontsource         SIL Open Font License 1.1

Each package's license ships with it in node_modules.
